  "query_preview": "..\nDry conditions are now expected for all the Marianas through Friday,\nwith the exception of island effect showers possible for all islands\nTuesday, as winds continue to weaken. These will likely remain \nshallow and short lived in nature due to dry air in the upper levels \nof the atmosphere. Some island effect is possible Monday but looks to\nremain mostly offshore due to light northwest winds. By Friday night,\nrainbands ahead of Invest 96W, currently north of Kosrae, may begin \nto move into the region and bring scattered showers and isolated \nthunderstorms. By Saturday night or sometime Sunday, heavier showers \nand thunderstorms will be possible along with gusty winds. However, \nthe track and intensity of 96W is highly uncertain as the system has \nyet to organize and remains at least a week out. Residents in the \nMarianas should continue to monitor forecasts over the next several \ndays, and maintain a general state of preparedness. See the \"Tropical\nSystems\" section for more details on 96W.",
